      "message": "The \"payload\" actually refers to the message part of the fernet token. self.crypto.decrypt() verifies the fernet token HMAC, decrypts the message/payload, and returns the integrity-verified payload. All that to say that the proposed validation error message is slightly misleading: it\u0027s not a valid fernet token for some reason (we haven\u0027t tried to recognize the payload itself yet): it might not be a fernet token at all, it might be encrypted with a key that we don\u0027t trust, the HMAC integrity verification might have failed, etc.\n\ntl;dr I think if you change the word \"payload\" to \"token,\" then it\u0027ll be perfectly accurate.",
